      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© owned by Center for Academic Publications Japan (Publisher).",
        "AbstractText": "Hemolytic activity of the culture supernatant of Leptospira interrogans serovar canicola strain Moulton grown in protein-free medium was demonstrated. The activity began to appear in the late logarithmic phase of growth of the organism and reached a plateau after 2 weeks of cultivation. It was inactivated by the addition of dipotassium ethylenediaminetetraacetate, but was effectively restored by Mg2+ . Hemolysis by the culture supernatant was stimulated by \"hot-cold\" incubation. Sheep erythrocytes treated with the culture supernatant of the organism were transformed into spherocytes, in which invagination was observed. A hemolysin inhibitor in rabbit serum was found to be in the chloroform-methanol soluble fraction of the serum. The hemolysin of Leptospira may be phospholipase C."
      },
